WEBVTT

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.561
There was another
antiwar demonstration

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.539
at the UC-Santa Cruz campus
last night.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.598
Tear gas was used

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.973
to disperse the crowd
of 3,000 angry students.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.536
The temperature right now
in downtown Barstow

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.808
is 75 degrees.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.917
Whoa, whoa.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.388
Far out.

00:02:56.874 --> 00:02:58.000
Come in.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.538
Sorry, Tuvok.

00:03:00.578 --> 00:03:02.671
I was just practicing
my serve.

00:03:02.714 --> 00:03:03.738
Your "serve?"

00:03:03.781 --> 00:03:04.941
Tennis.

00:03:05.049 --> 00:03:07.574
After 19 years, I've decided
to take it up again.

00:03:07.618 --> 00:03:08.949
I'm a little rusty.

00:03:09.053 --> 00:03:11.419
I played in a novice tournament
on the holodeck.

00:03:11.456 --> 00:03:13.720
I lost my first match
in straight sets.

00:03:13.758 --> 00:03:17.319
Perhaps if you maintained
eye contact with the ball

00:03:17.362 --> 00:03:18.954
at the apex of its trajectory,

00:03:18.996 --> 00:03:20.588
your serve would be
more effective.

00:03:20.631 --> 00:03:22.394
You play tennis?

00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:24.230
Simple physics, Captain.

00:03:24.268 --> 00:03:27.294
Not as simple as when I played
on the high school tennis team.

00:03:27.338 --> 00:03:29.101
What can I do for you, Tuvok?

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.631
I've completed my monthly
security evaluation.

00:03:31.676 --> 00:03:32.768
All systems and crew are...

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:33.777
Red Alert.

00:03:33.811 --> 00:03:34.937
Captain Janeway to the Bridge.

00:03:37.615 --> 00:03:39.310
Report.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.318
Some sort of spatial rift.

00:03:41.352 --> 00:03:42.580
It opened right in front of us.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:43.985
Analysis.

00:03:44.088 --> 00:03:46.113
It's a distortion
in the space-time continuum,

00:03:46.157 --> 00:03:48.216
but it's got
a graviton matrix.

00:03:48.259 --> 00:03:49.920
It's being artificially
generated.

00:03:49.961 --> 00:03:50.928
By whom?

00:03:50.962 --> 00:03:52.190
Sensors can't get inside.

00:03:53.231 --> 00:03:55.096
The distortion
field's fluctuating.

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:56.566
Something's coming out.

00:03:58.603 --> 00:04:00.594
It appears to be a small ship...

00:04:00.638 --> 00:04:02.071
approximately six meters
in length.

00:04:02.106 --> 00:04:03.733
Magnify.

00:04:06.077 --> 00:04:09.308
Sensors are reading
one occupant... human.

00:04:09.347 --> 00:04:11.611
He is holding position
at the perimeter of the rift.

00:04:11.649 --> 00:04:14.345
There's a subspace signature
emanating from the ship.

00:04:16.821 --> 00:04:18.948
Captain...

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.686
it's Federation.

00:04:23.027 --> 00:04:23.994
Hail them.

00:04:25.029 --> 00:04:25.961
No response.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:27.964
They appear
to be charging weapons.

00:04:27.999 --> 00:04:28.966
Shields up.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.262
Hail them again.

00:04:37.575 --> 00:04:38.735
Shields are down.

00:04:38.776 --> 00:04:39.504
Get us out of here.

00:04:39.544 --> 00:04:41.774
Helm control is off-line.

00:04:41.813 --> 00:04:43.974
He's firing some kind
of subatomic disruptor.

00:04:44.048 --> 00:04:45.140
Return fire.

00:04:45.183 --> 00:04:46.480
Full phasers.

00:04:46.517 --> 00:04:48.246
No effect.

00:04:49.153 --> 00:04:50.415
Voyager's molecular structure

00:04:50.455 --> 00:04:51.422
is coming apart!

00:04:51.456 --> 00:04:52.980
Tuvok, divert
all available power

00:04:53.057 --> 00:04:53.989
to the deflector.

00:04:54.058 --> 00:04:55.719
Send out a high-energy
polaron pulse.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.819
It might help
to disrupt his weapon.

00:04:57.862 --> 00:05:00.296
Emitting deflector pulse...
now.

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:04.464
It's working.

00:05:04.502 --> 00:05:05.935
We are being hailed.

00:05:06.037 --> 00:05:07.937
On screen.

00:05:07.972 --> 00:05:09.906
Starship Voyager,
I'm Captain Braxton

00:05:09.941 --> 00:05:11.670
of the Federation Timeship Aeon.

00:05:11.709 --> 00:05:14.041
I've come from 29th century
Earth, 500 years

00:05:14.078 --> 00:05:15.045
into your future.

00:05:15.079 --> 00:05:17.172
Please disengage
your deflector pulse.

00:05:17.215 --> 00:05:19.115
Why are you firing at us?

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.311
Your vessel is responsible
for a disaster in my century...

00:05:21.352 --> 00:05:22.785
a temporal explosion
that will destroy

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.082
all of Earth's solar system.

00:05:24.121 --> 00:05:26.817
I've come back in time
to prevent that occurrence.

00:05:26.858 --> 00:05:28.382
My mission is your destruction.

00:05:28.426 --> 00:05:30.223
You must not resist.

00:05:30.261 --> 00:05:31.819
I'm going to need
some more information

00:05:31.863 --> 00:05:32.955
before I allow you...

00:05:33.064 --> 00:05:34.156
Debris
from your secondary hull

00:05:34.198 --> 00:05:35.222
was found in the explosion.

00:05:35.266 --> 00:05:36.255
Captain, I simply...

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.392
No time!

00:05:39.971 --> 00:05:42.769
He's remodulating
the subatomic disruptor.

00:05:42.807 --> 00:05:44.604
Our deflector is losing power.

00:05:44.642 --> 00:05:45.973
It won't hold much longer.

00:05:46.077 --> 00:05:47.408
Captain, if he's
telling the truth...

00:05:47.445 --> 00:05:48.912
I won't sacrifice
this ship and crew

00:05:48.946 --> 00:05:50.379
based on a ten second
conversation.

00:05:50.414 --> 00:05:52.109
I need proof.

00:05:53.584 --> 00:05:54.983
It doesn't look like
we're going to get it.

00:05:55.052 --> 00:05:57.282
Adjust our deflector to match
the frequency of his weapon.

00:05:57.321 --> 00:05:58.788
Try to overload his emitter.

00:06:00.758 --> 00:06:02.555
It seems to be working.

00:06:02.593 --> 00:06:05.426
His weapon is off-line
and his ship has been damaged.

00:06:05.463 --> 00:06:07.021
The rift is destabilizing

00:06:07.064 --> 00:06:08.895
and he's being pulled
back inside.

00:06:08.933 --> 00:06:10.230
Reestablish helm control.

00:06:10.268 --> 00:06:11.599
I'm trying, Captain,

00:06:11.636 --> 00:06:14.264
but we seem to be caught in some
kind of graviton distortion.

00:06:14.305 --> 00:06:16.273
We're being pulled in, too.

00:06:32.189 --> 00:06:33.656
Status.

00:06:33.691 --> 00:06:36.785
Primary systems
are coming back on line.

00:06:36.827 --> 00:06:39.193
The weapons grid and power array
took heavy damage.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.130
The temporal rift is closed.

00:06:41.165 --> 00:06:42.291
Where are we?

00:06:48.873 --> 00:06:50.738
Home.

00:06:52.209 --> 00:06:54.439
We just cut across
half the galaxy.

00:06:54.478 --> 00:06:57.311
The rift must have
originated here.

00:06:57.348 --> 00:07:00.442
Hail Starfleet Command.

00:07:01.886 --> 00:07:04.218
No response
on standard frequencies.

00:07:04.255 --> 00:07:06.189
Curious.

00:07:06.223 --> 00:07:09.681
I am picking up a multitude
of narrow-band EM signals.

00:07:09.727 --> 00:07:11.092
Let's hear.

00:07:12.363 --> 00:07:13.352
Hello, Mom...

00:07:13.397 --> 00:07:14.659
There's no commercial
interruptions...

00:07:14.699 --> 00:07:15.893
If you leave
a message at the beep,

00:07:15.933 --> 00:07:16.900
I'll get right back to you.

00:07:16.934 --> 00:07:19.061
Robertson takes a hard left...

00:07:28.212 --> 00:07:30.806
The question isn't where we are.

00:07:30.848 --> 00:07:32.941
It's when we are.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.039
Mr. Kim?

00:07:34.852 --> 00:07:37.286
According to astrometric
readings...

00:07:40.024 --> 00:07:42.720
the year is 1996.

00:07:44.528 --> 00:07:45.620
The late 20th century.

00:07:45.663 --> 00:07:46.789
Captain.

00:07:46.831 --> 00:07:49.356
They had surveillance
satellites during this time.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.958
Maintain a high orbit.

00:07:51.068 --> 00:07:53.536
And modulate the shields
to scatter their radar.

00:07:53.571 --> 00:07:55.061
We don't want
to alarm the natives.

00:07:55.106 --> 00:07:56.937
What about the timeship?

00:07:56.974 --> 00:07:57.941
Is it here, too?

00:07:57.975 --> 00:07:59.966
There's no sign
of the vessel in orbit.

00:08:00.077 --> 00:08:01.567
Scanning the planet's surface.

00:08:02.647 --> 00:08:04.911
I am picking up low-frequency
subspace readings

00:08:04.982 --> 00:08:06.916
emanating
from the northern hemisphere.

00:08:06.951 --> 00:08:08.748
Subspace technology
shouldn't exist

00:08:08.786 --> 00:08:10.219
for another 100 years or so.

00:08:10.254 --> 00:08:12.245
Could be our friend
from the 29th century.

00:08:12.289 --> 00:08:14.086
Localize it.

00:08:14.125 --> 00:08:15.854
North American continent.

00:08:15.893 --> 00:08:17.451
Pacific coast.

00:08:17.495 --> 00:08:20.589
The city of... Los Angeles.

00:08:24.201 --> 00:08:26.192
We've got to go down there.

00:08:26.237 --> 00:08:29.695
If it is Captain Braxton,
he's the key to all this.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:32.937
And at the moment, his ship
is the only way we have

00:08:33.044 --> 00:08:34.375
of getting back
to our own century.

00:08:34.412 --> 00:08:36.937
Chakotay, Tuvok, Paris,
you're with me.

00:08:37.048 --> 00:08:40.711
Mr. Kim, you have the Bridge.

00:08:40.751 --> 00:08:42.241
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:42.286 --> 00:08:43.878
As I recall, Tom,
you're something

00:08:43.921 --> 00:08:46.355
of an aficionado
on 20th century America.

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:47.414
That's right.

00:08:47.458 --> 00:08:49.722
What will we need to pass
as locals in this era?

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.594
Simple. Nice clothes,
fast car and lots of money.

00:08:58.769 --> 00:09:00.361
Hey, buddy, look what you did.

00:09:02.707 --> 00:09:03.935
Sorry, man.

00:09:20.391 --> 00:09:23.519
We could have worn
our Starfleet uniforms.

00:09:23.561 --> 00:09:25.426
I doubt if anyone
would have noticed.

00:09:33.771 --> 00:09:35.898
The subspace readings
are coming from

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:38.340
within a hundred-meter
radius of our position,

00:09:38.375 --> 00:09:39.933
but I can't pinpoint the source.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.240
I find it hard to believe
a ship from the 29th century

00:09:42.279 --> 00:09:44.110
could've landed on this beach
without being noticed.

00:09:44.148 --> 00:09:45.843
We have no idea
what kind of technology

00:09:45.883 --> 00:09:47.282
they might have in the future.

00:09:47.318 --> 00:09:48.285
Maybe it's cloaked.

00:09:48.319 --> 00:09:49.286
Let's spread out.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.618
Tuvok, Paris,
go check the shoreline.

00:09:51.655 --> 00:09:53.418
Chakotay and I
will search the boardwalk.

00:09:53.457 --> 00:09:54.424
Aye, Captain.

00:09:54.458 --> 00:09:57.450
Well, Kathryn, you got us home.

00:09:57.495 --> 00:10:00.293
Right place... wrong time.

00:10:00.331 --> 00:10:02.799
But it is good to be back,
nevertheless.

00:10:02.833 --> 00:10:04.960
Maybe I should look up
a few ancestors.

00:10:05.069 --> 00:10:07.435
As I recall, one of them
was a schoolteacher in Arizona.

00:10:07.471 --> 00:10:08.961
I don't know what
my relatives were doing

00:10:09.039 --> 00:10:10.063
this far back in history...

00:10:10.107 --> 00:10:11.631
Coming through.
Sorry.

00:10:11.675 --> 00:10:14.769
For all I know, she could be
my great, great, great...

00:10:14.812 --> 00:10:16.677
great grandmother.

00:10:16.714 --> 00:10:18.306
She does have your legs.

00:10:18.349 --> 00:10:19.316
Have you ever been

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:20.715
to Southern California,
Chakotay?

00:10:20.751 --> 00:10:21.877
No.

00:10:21.919 --> 00:10:24.080
After the Hermosa Quake in 2047,

00:10:24.121 --> 00:10:27.181
this entire region sank
under 200 meters of water.

00:10:27.224 --> 00:10:29.419
It became one of the world's
largest coral reefs,

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.690
home to thousands
of different marine species.

00:10:33.631 --> 00:10:36.896
Some... interesting species
in this century.

00:10:45.575 --> 00:10:47.736
Subspace readings
are weaker here.

00:10:47.777 --> 00:10:49.210
Let's head up to the boardwalk.

00:10:52.281 --> 00:10:54.306
Ah... the sun feels great.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.341
Thermal and ultraviolet
radiation

00:10:56.385 --> 00:10:57.716
are at hazardous levels.

00:10:57.754 --> 00:10:59.915
Oh, lighten up, Tuvok.

00:10:59.956 --> 00:11:01.821
This was a great time and place

00:11:01.858 --> 00:11:03.792
and you're getting
to see it firsthand.

00:11:03.826 --> 00:11:05.225
Come on, take off your shirt.

00:11:05.261 --> 00:11:07.821
And risk dermal dysplasia?
No, thank you.

00:11:07.864 --> 00:11:09.422
Vulcans... deep down

00:11:09.465 --> 00:11:11.330
you're all a bunch
of hypochondriacs.

00:11:13.703 --> 00:11:16.069
The readings are coming
from over there.

00:11:16.105 --> 00:11:17.094
Ten meters...

00:11:18.741 --> 00:11:19.867
There.

00:11:24.914 --> 00:11:26.381
So much for the timeship.

00:11:26.415 --> 00:11:28.280
There's no doubt about it.

00:11:28.317 --> 00:11:31.377
The subspace readings
are coming from him.

00:12:25.041 --> 00:12:26.531
No way.

00:12:43.092 --> 00:12:44.753
Way.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.358
It's crap.

00:12:49.398 --> 00:12:51.389
The component density
is too low,

00:12:51.434 --> 00:12:52.799
the voltage variance
is out of spec

00:12:52.835 --> 00:12:53.927
and I don't even like the color.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:55.164
But, Mr. Starling...

00:12:55.204 --> 00:12:56.228
We've got less than six months

00:12:56.272 --> 00:12:58.763
before we introduce
the HyperPro PC.

00:12:58.808 --> 00:13:00.298
And with a chip like
this driving it,

00:13:00.343 --> 00:13:02.607
we'll have to change
the name to "Edsel."

00:13:04.113 --> 00:13:05.603
I gave your company
this contract

00:13:05.648 --> 00:13:07.513
because you're the best
in the business.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.575
Next to us, of course.

00:13:11.053 --> 00:13:12.077
Go home, Jim.

00:13:12.121 --> 00:13:14.316
Lose some sleep over this.

00:13:14.357 --> 00:13:16.291
I want a full report
middle of next week.

00:13:18.928 --> 00:13:20.225
What am I doing, Dave?

00:13:20.263 --> 00:13:21.355
You're in a meeting, sir.

00:13:21.397 --> 00:13:22.591
And?

00:13:22.632 --> 00:13:24.657
And I know
I'm not supposed to interrupt,

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.328
but there's a woman
calling on line three

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:30.134
from Griffith Observatory...
a Rain Robinson.

00:13:30.172 --> 00:13:31.662
She says it's urgent.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:35.468
Put her through.

00:13:38.781 --> 00:13:40.146
Henry Starling.

00:13:40.182 --> 00:13:41.149
Hi.

00:13:41.183 --> 00:13:42.741
I don't know if you remember me.

00:13:42.785 --> 00:13:45.686
I'm one of the astronomers
at the SETI lab you're funding.

00:13:45.721 --> 00:13:47.712
We met at the Griffith
restoration party.

00:13:47.757 --> 00:13:49.190
Yes, yes. What is it?

00:13:49.225 --> 00:13:51.659
Okay. Well, it was
my understanding

00:13:51.694 --> 00:13:53.389
you wanted to be notified
immediately

00:13:53.429 --> 00:13:55.226
if I ever picked up
a gamma emission

00:13:55.264 --> 00:13:57.824
that matched the frequency
profile you gave me.

00:13:57.867 --> 00:14:00.836
Well... I did.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.838
So... I am.

00:14:04.674 --> 00:14:05.641
Are you certain?

00:14:05.675 --> 00:14:07.506
Positive.
I tracked the emission,

00:14:07.543 --> 00:14:08.510
and guess what?

00:14:08.544 --> 00:14:10.068
The source is in orbit.

00:14:10.112 --> 00:14:11.511
It is right above us.

00:14:11.547 --> 00:14:13.105
When did it show up?

00:14:13.149 --> 00:14:16.243
Uh... according to the raw data,

00:14:16.285 --> 00:14:18.150
about 90 minutes ago.

00:14:18.187 --> 00:14:19.245
I'm not picking up anything

00:14:19.288 --> 00:14:21.518
from the standard
search parameters.

00:14:21.557 --> 00:14:24.082
Wow. That means
no one else knows

00:14:24.126 --> 00:14:25.388
there's something up there.

00:14:25.428 --> 00:14:26.952
We have got to tell somebody
about this.

00:14:27.063 --> 00:14:27.961
We've got to call NASA!

00:14:28.064 --> 00:14:31.192
Rain, that's a little premature,
don't you think?

00:14:31.233 --> 00:14:33.531
This could be a close encounter,

00:14:33.569 --> 00:14:35.503
but then again,
could be a flock of geese.

00:14:35.538 --> 00:14:37.665
Mm... geese
don't park themselves

00:14:37.707 --> 00:14:40.540
20,000 kilometers
above North America.

00:14:40.576 --> 00:14:43.773
Let's send a message up there,
see if there's a response.

00:14:43.813 --> 00:14:47.249
No, no. We don't know
what we've found,

00:14:47.283 --> 00:14:50.650
and until we do, I'm not going
to risk embarrassing myself

00:14:50.686 --> 00:14:52.210
or your observatory.

00:14:52.254 --> 00:14:54.154
Track the emission,
collect more data

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:55.282
and keep me informed.

00:14:55.324 --> 00:14:56.951
In the meantime,

00:14:56.993 --> 00:14:59.518
I'm going to put
a bottle of champagne on ice.

00:14:59.562 --> 00:15:01.757
Do you think E.T.
Likes Chateau Coeur?

00:15:01.797 --> 00:15:04.857
Well, if he doesn't, I've got
a six-pack in the fridge.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.060
Good work, Rain.

00:15:06.102 --> 00:15:07.626
Stay in touch.

00:15:35.197 --> 00:15:37.995
Oh, what the hell.

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.537
Anyone up there?

00:15:55.084 --> 00:15:56.574
That trip through the rift

00:15:56.619 --> 00:15:58.553
is still affecting
our primary systems.

00:15:58.587 --> 00:16:02.785
Weapons are off-line,
we blew three EPS conduits

00:16:02.825 --> 00:16:05.589
and our main transporter
buffer just crashed.

00:16:05.628 --> 00:16:07.220
We've got an away team
down there.

00:16:07.263 --> 00:16:10.391
I know. We've still got
emergency transporters,

00:16:10.433 --> 00:16:12.025
but they're short-range.

00:16:12.068 --> 00:16:13.695
How close to the surface
would we have to get

00:16:13.736 --> 00:16:15.169
to beam them up?

00:16:15.204 --> 00:16:17.798
Pretty close. I'd say
less than ten kilometers.

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:19.364
If we do that, somebody's
going to see us.

00:16:19.408 --> 00:16:23.208
Sir, I'm picking up an EM signal
from the planet's surface.

00:16:23.245 --> 00:16:25.304
It's directed
at our coordinates.

00:16:25.347 --> 00:16:27.247
On screen.

00:16:27.283 --> 00:16:29.843
Greetings from the people
of Earth.

00:16:37.259 --> 00:16:39.250
Shall I respond, sir?

00:16:39.295 --> 00:16:40.819
Absolutely not.

00:16:52.908 --> 00:16:55.638
He appears to live
on the street.

00:16:55.678 --> 00:16:58.408
That pushcart seems to
contain all his belongings.

00:16:58.447 --> 00:17:00.506
From what we can tell,
he spends most of his time

00:17:00.549 --> 00:17:02.574
putting up literature
about the end of the world.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:06.954
Hello? Hello?

00:17:10.326 --> 00:17:11.350
Janeway here.

00:17:11.393 --> 00:17:12.792
Captain, we've got a problem.

00:17:12.828 --> 00:17:14.386
We received a signal
from the surface.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:15.795
It looks like
a standard greeting

00:17:15.831 --> 00:17:17.731
designed for extraterrestrials.

00:17:17.766 --> 00:17:18.926
We've been detected.

00:17:19.001 --> 00:17:19.933
It looks that way.

00:17:20.002 --> 00:17:22.163
We tracked the signal
to an observatory

00:17:22.204 --> 00:17:24.069
about 20 kilometers
from your location.

00:17:24.106 --> 00:17:26.438
Transport Paris and Tuvok
to those coordinates.

00:17:26.475 --> 00:17:27.669
I can't do that right now,

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.405
not without going
into a lower orbit.

00:17:29.445 --> 00:17:31.606
The main pattern buffer
is off-line.

00:17:31.647 --> 00:17:33.444
B'Elanna says it could take
a couple of days to repair.

00:17:33.482 --> 00:17:34.847
In that case,

00:17:34.884 --> 00:17:37.444
transmit those coordinates
to Mr. Tuvok's tricorder.

00:17:37.486 --> 00:17:39.579
He and Tom will have
to get there using more...

00:17:39.622 --> 00:17:41.749
conventional means.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.156
Aye, Captain. Kim out.

00:17:44.193 --> 00:17:46.320
Nobody walks in Los Angeles,

00:17:46.362 --> 00:17:48.956
and they don't have much of a
public transportation system.

00:17:49.064 --> 00:17:50.122
We're going to need some wheels.

00:17:50.166 --> 00:17:51.497
Do what you have to do.

00:17:51.534 --> 00:17:54.332
Find out who sent that message
and get more information.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.668
Have we been detected?
How many people know about us?

00:17:56.705 --> 00:17:58.570
We cannot risk
contaminating the timeline.

00:17:58.607 --> 00:17:59.574
Aye, Captain.

00:17:59.608 --> 00:18:00.700
See you later.

00:18:37.644 --> 00:18:38.941
Who the hell are you?!

00:18:38.978 --> 00:18:40.036
This is my stuff!

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:42.173
It's all right.
We don't want your stuff.

00:18:42.215 --> 00:18:44.206
We just want to ask you
a few questions.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:45.376
No!

00:18:45.418 --> 00:18:47.215
No, no, no!
No more questions!

00:18:47.253 --> 00:18:49.585
No. No more surveys!

00:18:49.622 --> 00:18:52.682
Damn social workers
coming around all the time!

00:18:52.726 --> 00:18:54.318
No, I don't need your advice!

00:18:54.361 --> 00:18:55.760
I don't need your...

00:19:02.469 --> 00:19:03.959
Voyager...

00:19:05.238 --> 00:19:06.296
I knew you'd show up.

00:19:06.339 --> 00:19:08.034
Oh, this is all your fault.

00:19:08.074 --> 00:19:09.439
This is all your doing!

00:19:11.111 --> 00:19:12.544
Captain Braxton?

00:19:12.579 --> 00:19:15.139
I told you to turn off
your deflector pulse,

00:19:15.181 --> 00:19:16.910
but you wouldn't listen to me!

00:19:16.983 --> 00:19:19.474
Voyager! Fools!

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:24.548
Captain, what's happened to you?

00:19:24.591 --> 00:19:25.922
The last time we saw you...

00:19:26.025 --> 00:19:28.357
I was a younger man,
confident in my mission!

00:19:28.395 --> 00:19:29.657
But you wouldn't listen to me.

00:19:29.696 --> 00:19:31.391
No, you were too concerned
with yourselves.

00:19:31.431 --> 00:19:32.921
You were trying to destroy us.

00:19:32.966 --> 00:19:34.934
I was trying to save
billions of lives...

00:19:34.968 --> 00:19:37.766
to stop a chain of reaction
that started with Voyager.

00:19:37.804 --> 00:19:39.032
But it's too late now.

00:19:39.072 --> 00:19:41.802
All things are set in motion.

00:19:41.841 --> 00:19:43.468
The temporal explosion
will occur.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:46.035
The end is coming!
The future's end!

00:19:46.079 --> 00:19:47.671
Captain, how long
have you been here...

00:19:47.714 --> 00:19:48.874
in the 20th century?

00:19:48.915 --> 00:19:50.041
Oh, too long.

00:19:50.083 --> 00:19:51.914
30 years too long.

00:19:51.951 --> 00:19:53.942
And yet we just arrived. Why?

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:55.954
Pure chance.

00:19:56.022 --> 00:19:58.047
When you knocked my navigation
system off course,

00:19:58.091 --> 00:20:01.356
there's no telling
where we would have ended up.

00:20:01.394 --> 00:20:02.952
Who's been here?

00:20:02.996 --> 00:20:04.429
Who took my pencils?

00:20:04.464 --> 00:20:07.627
Oh! Always something missing.

00:20:09.035 --> 00:20:10.969
People always wanting
to steal things.

00:20:11.004 --> 00:20:13.404
Greedy people!

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.271
Postindustrial barbarians!

00:20:15.308 --> 00:20:17.799
Captain, we want to help you,

00:20:17.844 --> 00:20:20.074
but you've got to give us
more information.

00:20:20.113 --> 00:20:22.946
You said that Voyager
causes the explosion.

00:20:22.982 --> 00:20:24.677
Yes.

00:20:24.717 --> 00:20:26.582
No...

00:20:26.619 --> 00:20:29.281
and yes.

00:20:29.322 --> 00:20:31.256
That's a paradox, my dear.

00:20:31.291 --> 00:20:34.089
"A" leads to "B"
leads to "C" leads to "A."

00:20:37.864 --> 00:20:38.990
Juvenile minds.

00:20:39.098 --> 00:20:41.896
Oh, how can I
make you understand, huh?

00:20:41.935 --> 00:20:46.998
A) There's an explosion
in the 29th century.

00:20:47.106 --> 00:20:49.597
Debris from Voyager's hull
is found in evidence.

00:20:49.642 --> 00:20:52.634
I go back in time
to destroy you.

00:20:54.581 --> 00:20:58.210
B) You try to stop me,
disabling my weapon,

00:20:58.251 --> 00:21:02.381
which causes me to crash-land
back here in the 20th century.

00:21:03.823 --> 00:21:08.055
C) Someone in this century

00:21:08.094 --> 00:21:11.063
steals my timeship
and launches it.

00:21:11.097 --> 00:21:13.725
They go into the future,
and once there,

00:21:13.766 --> 00:21:16.291
they make one critical mistake,

00:21:16.336 --> 00:21:19.328
which causes
a temporal explosion

00:21:19.372 --> 00:21:24.639
that takes us
all the way back to "A."

00:21:24.677 --> 00:21:27.111
There's an explosion
in the 29th century.

00:21:27.146 --> 00:21:29.740
The cycle of causality
is complete.

00:21:29.782 --> 00:21:31.613
How do you know all this?

00:21:31.651 --> 00:21:34.552
What evidence do you have
that it will be your timeship

00:21:34.587 --> 00:21:36.384
that causes the disaster?

00:21:36.422 --> 00:21:40.085
I've spent 30 years answering
that very question.

00:21:46.799 --> 00:21:49.859
Oh, yes. When the explosion
first happened,

00:21:49.903 --> 00:21:53.270
my sensors recorded a whole
variety of chronometric data.

00:21:56.009 --> 00:21:57.237
The pulses were highly chaotic.

00:21:57.277 --> 00:22:00.178
At first, I thought
it was a warp core implosion,

00:22:00.213 --> 00:22:02.511
but then I found
debris from Voyager

00:22:02.549 --> 00:22:04.449
and my theory
seemed to be confirmed.

00:22:04.484 --> 00:22:05.576
It was you.

00:22:05.618 --> 00:22:08.951
But then, someone here
stole my timeship.

00:22:09.022 --> 00:22:11.388
Then it started to dawn on me.

00:22:11.424 --> 00:22:14.689
If someone were to fly
my timeship into the future

00:22:14.727 --> 00:22:17.161
without recalibrating
the temporal matrix,

00:22:17.196 --> 00:22:19.164
then that could cause
the kind of explosion

00:22:19.198 --> 00:22:21.189
that I witnessed
in the 29th century.

00:22:21.234 --> 00:22:23.429
So it really wasn't Voyager
after all.

00:22:23.469 --> 00:22:26.165
No. No, no, I reconstructed

00:22:26.205 --> 00:22:29.641
all the chronometric data
as best I could remember it

00:22:29.676 --> 00:22:32.372
and it proved that I was right.

00:22:32.412 --> 00:22:35.142
My ship causes the catastrophe.

00:22:35.181 --> 00:22:39.049
Which raises the question:
Who has your timeship?

00:22:41.287 --> 00:22:42.413
Starling.

00:22:42.455 --> 00:22:45.788
Henry Starling, CEO,

00:22:45.825 --> 00:22:46.985
Chronowerx Industries.

00:22:47.026 --> 00:22:51.122
Philanthropist, entrepreneur,
outstanding citizen. Ha!

00:22:51.164 --> 00:22:53.860
Before I crashed
in the year 1967,

00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:56.425
I made an emergency beam-out,
but he

00:22:56.469 --> 00:22:59.302
found my ship before I did
in some remote mountain range.

00:22:59.339 --> 00:23:02.433
I've been following this corrupt
little man ever since,

00:23:02.475 --> 00:23:06.206
tracking his movements,
but he's become too powerful.

00:23:06.245 --> 00:23:09.078
I can't get close to him.

00:23:09.115 --> 00:23:11.675
Of course,
you can't accomplish anything

00:23:11.718 --> 00:23:13.208
in this wretched century.

00:23:13.252 --> 00:23:14.844
Nobody here listens.

00:23:14.887 --> 00:23:19.415
Do you know that once, they
put me in a mental institution

00:23:19.459 --> 00:23:22.860
and filled me
with primitive pharmaceuticals?!

00:23:22.895 --> 00:23:25.329
Maybe we can help you
find Starling and your ship

00:23:25.365 --> 00:23:26.593
and get us back
to where we belong.

00:23:26.633 --> 00:23:28.624
No, I wouldn't do that
if I were you.

00:23:28.668 --> 00:23:29.828
Why not?

00:23:29.869 --> 00:23:30.927
Haven't you been listening?

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:32.528
"A" leads to "B"...

00:23:32.572 --> 00:23:34.130
Leads to "C", yes, we heard you.

00:23:34.173 --> 00:23:35.868
Why shouldn't we try
to stop Starling?

00:23:35.908 --> 00:23:39.400
Because somehow you're involved
in the disaster.

00:23:39.445 --> 00:23:41.538
That's why I found debris
from Voyager's hull

00:23:41.581 --> 00:23:43.446
at the explosion.

00:23:43.483 --> 00:23:45.883
You will be destroyed as well.

00:23:45.918 --> 00:23:47.613
Now that we know
what's going to happen,

00:23:47.654 --> 00:23:48.916
maybe we can figure out...

00:23:54.527 --> 00:23:55.755
Hey, Captain.

00:23:55.795 --> 00:23:57.660
How you doing?

00:23:57.697 --> 00:23:58.994
I understand you been putting

00:23:59.098 --> 00:24:01.396
these signs up
around the city again.

00:24:01.434 --> 00:24:02.560
No. No, no, no.

00:24:02.602 --> 00:24:04.661
Not me. I...
I would never do that.

00:24:04.704 --> 00:24:06.797
Why don't you walk over here
and we can talk about it?

00:24:06.839 --> 00:24:07.931
You stay right where you are!

00:24:08.007 --> 00:24:10.100
You quasi-Cardassian
totalitarian!

00:24:10.143 --> 00:24:11.576
Hey, look, no need
to get upset about this.

00:24:11.611 --> 00:24:13.101
We just want to talk to you
about the signs.

00:24:13.146 --> 00:24:14.807
Now, there've been
a few people complaining.

00:24:14.847 --> 00:24:17.714
Captain, tell them
I'm not crazy.

00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:19.775
Tell them I'm from the future.

00:24:22.321 --> 00:24:24.380
They came from the future, too,
you know.

00:24:24.424 --> 00:24:25.755
Okay.

00:24:25.792 --> 00:24:27.282
Yeah, they came in
on a starship.

00:24:27.326 --> 00:24:28.850
All right.

00:24:32.331 --> 00:24:33.320
Traitors!

00:24:34.934 --> 00:24:36.799
Okay, yeah.
Oh, stand by.

00:24:36.836 --> 00:24:38.633
This is 247-Baker,
in foot pursuit

00:24:38.671 --> 00:24:39.695
of a 51-50 suspect.

00:24:39.739 --> 00:24:41.730
We'll have to worry
about him later.

00:24:41.774 --> 00:24:44.766
Right now,
we've got to find Starling.

00:24:49.982 --> 00:24:52.416
We're not quite at
the little green men stage yet,

00:24:52.452 --> 00:24:54.613
but believe me,
you'll be the first to know.

00:24:54.654 --> 00:24:56.087
What I think we have here

00:24:56.122 --> 00:24:58.716
is an overenthusiastic
young lady.

00:24:58.758 --> 00:25:00.658
I'm afraid she's exaggerating.

00:25:00.693 --> 00:25:02.456
We don't have anything.
Not yet.

00:25:03.463 --> 00:25:04.953
Thank you, Professor.

00:25:07.433 --> 00:25:09.424
You know what
that little brat did?

00:25:09.469 --> 00:25:12.461
She E-mailed a friend of hers
at JPL.

00:25:12.505 --> 00:25:15.338
Who called his professor
at Cal Tech.

00:25:15.374 --> 00:25:17.365
She's a security risk.

00:25:17.410 --> 00:25:20.174
Go to Griffith, get the data,
get rid of her.

00:25:20.213 --> 00:25:21.475
Yes, sir.

00:25:21.514 --> 00:25:23.072
Dunbar.

00:25:23.116 --> 00:25:25.277
If it's true... if they're here...

00:25:25.318 --> 00:25:27.878
it's only a matter of time
before they find me.

00:25:27.920 --> 00:25:30.855
There's no telling
what capabilities they'll have.

00:25:30.890 --> 00:25:33.120
You may have to use the weapon.

00:25:33.159 --> 00:25:34.751
I understand.

00:25:59.952 --> 00:26:02.648
Perhaps we should find
a more secluded parking place.

00:26:02.688 --> 00:26:04.918
This is, after all,
a stolen vehicle.

00:26:05.024 --> 00:26:06.719
Nobody's around, Tuvok.

00:26:06.759 --> 00:26:07.919
We're fine.

00:26:07.960 --> 00:26:09.154
A taxicab

00:26:09.195 --> 00:26:11.288
would have been less worrisome
and more ethical.

00:26:11.330 --> 00:26:12.558
We haven't stolen anything.

00:26:12.598 --> 00:26:13.929
We borrowed a car

00:26:13.966 --> 00:26:15.297
and we'll return it
to the dealership

00:26:15.334 --> 00:26:16.301
as soon as we're done.

00:26:16.335 --> 00:26:18.599
I was referring to the ethics
of time travel.

00:26:18.638 --> 00:26:20.765
Somehow, I doubt
that taking a test drive

00:26:20.807 --> 00:26:23.207
is going to alter
the course of the universe.

00:26:54.707 --> 00:26:56.402
Over here.

00:26:56.442 --> 00:26:59.775
These are radio wave readouts.

00:27:04.650 --> 00:27:07.210
It looks like radio
telescope transmissions.

00:27:07.253 --> 00:27:08.447
Pretty basic.

00:27:08.487 --> 00:27:09.886
Lieutenant,
you are being careless.

00:27:09.922 --> 00:27:11.685
- Tuvok...
- I will not

00:27:11.724 --> 00:27:12.918
lighten up on this matter.

00:27:13.025 --> 00:27:15.687
Thus far, I have tolerated
your impulsive methods.

00:27:15.728 --> 00:27:17.923
At times, they do
work to our advantage,

00:27:18.030 --> 00:27:20.931
but discretion is also a virtue.

00:27:20.966 --> 00:27:23.560
We must leave things
exactly as they were.

00:27:30.309 --> 00:27:31.936
They've found us, all right.

00:27:32.011 --> 00:27:35.037
The orbital schematic
matches Voyager's position.

00:27:35.081 --> 00:27:37.174
According to this data,
they are tracking

00:27:37.216 --> 00:27:39.013
the warp emissions
from our engines.

00:27:40.352 --> 00:27:42.684
Nobody in this century even
knows what warp emissions are.

00:27:42.721 --> 00:27:44.086
Nevertheless, it appears

00:27:44.123 --> 00:27:46.421
they've configured their
telescope to scan for them.

00:27:46.459 --> 00:27:48.757
Excuse me.

00:27:48.794 --> 00:27:50.955
"Do not enter",
"Employees only"...

00:27:51.063 --> 00:27:52.291
the sign on the door?

00:27:52.331 --> 00:27:53.889
Uh, I'm sorry.

00:27:53.933 --> 00:27:55.332
I think we're a little lost.

00:27:55.367 --> 00:27:57.358
We were on the museum tour,
and we took a wrong turn

00:27:57.403 --> 00:27:58.768
at the Saturn exhibit.

00:27:58.804 --> 00:28:01.102
Perhaps you could tell us
how to get back to the lobby.

00:28:02.208 --> 00:28:04.506
Go back down the hall,
take a left at Mars,

00:28:04.543 --> 00:28:05.567
right at Halley's comet

00:28:05.611 --> 00:28:07.010
and then just keep going
straight ahead

00:28:07.046 --> 00:28:09.173
past the soda machine, okay?

00:28:12.918 --> 00:28:14.909
This lab is, uh...

00:28:14.987 --> 00:28:16.955
pretty groovy.

00:28:18.023 --> 00:28:19.081
Groovy...

00:28:19.125 --> 00:28:20.615
What do you do here?

00:28:20.659 --> 00:28:22.524
We watch the skies.

00:28:22.561 --> 00:28:23.585
For what?

00:28:23.629 --> 00:28:25.790
Signs of extraterrestrial life.

00:28:25.831 --> 00:28:27.298
Nice meeting you.

00:28:31.737 --> 00:28:34.365
My name is Tom Paris,
by the way.

00:28:34.406 --> 00:28:36.340
Rain Robinson.

00:28:36.375 --> 00:28:39.867
Your curves don't look so great.

00:28:39.912 --> 00:28:40.936
Excuse me?

00:28:40.980 --> 00:28:44.245
This is a Fourier
spectral analysis?

00:28:44.283 --> 00:28:46.513
That's exactly what it is.

00:28:46.552 --> 00:28:48.577
You know, you might
get better resolution

00:28:48.621 --> 00:28:50.885
if you adjust
your amplitude parameters.

00:28:50.923 --> 00:28:53.858
You're probably right.

00:28:53.893 --> 00:28:56.657
Or you might try using
a theta band filter.

00:28:56.695 --> 00:28:58.788
You know a lot for someone

00:28:58.831 --> 00:29:00.799
who can't find his way
past Saturn.

00:29:00.833 --> 00:29:03.324
I majored in astrophysics.

00:29:03.369 --> 00:29:04.336
Where?

00:29:04.370 --> 00:29:05.837
Starfleet Academy.

00:29:05.871 --> 00:29:07.304
Never heard of it.

00:29:08.974 --> 00:29:10.407
Uh, East Coast school.

00:29:12.111 --> 00:29:14.306
Orgy of the Walking Dead?!

00:29:14.346 --> 00:29:16.075
That's a classic!

00:29:16.115 --> 00:29:20.142
Did you see the sequel, uh...
Bride of the Corpse?

00:29:20.186 --> 00:29:21.346
Let me guess.

00:29:21.387 --> 00:29:23.184
You minored in "B" movies.

00:29:23.222 --> 00:29:25.087
Something like that.

00:29:25.124 --> 00:29:26.614
Pardon me, Tom.

00:29:26.659 --> 00:29:27.887
We should be going.

00:29:27.927 --> 00:29:29.622
Our friends are waiting for us.

00:29:32.231 --> 00:29:33.357
Yeah, right.

00:29:35.801 --> 00:29:36.961
Got to go.

00:29:38.604 --> 00:29:39.593
Hey.

00:29:41.106 --> 00:29:42.937
Uh...

00:29:43.008 --> 00:29:46.500
I do the planetarium show
Tuesday nights,

00:29:46.545 --> 00:29:48.274
so, uh...
you guys should

00:29:48.314 --> 00:29:49.941
come by, check it out,

00:29:50.015 --> 00:29:51.778
bring your friends...

00:29:51.817 --> 00:29:55.150
"The best stars in Hollywood
are right above us."

00:29:55.187 --> 00:29:57.587
Yeah, great...

00:29:57.623 --> 00:30:01.650
but I think
we're busy on Tuesday.

00:30:01.694 --> 00:30:03.286
Thanks anyway.

00:30:08.701 --> 00:30:10.134
No problem.

00:30:17.209 --> 00:30:18.699
Whoa.

00:30:25.017 --> 00:30:27.815
I downloaded all of her data
into the tricorder

00:30:27.853 --> 00:30:29.650
and disrupted
her data storage device.

00:30:29.688 --> 00:30:32.179
Good. I hope she doesn't
get in any trouble.

00:30:32.224 --> 00:30:33.987
It will simply look like
a computer malfunction.

00:30:34.093 --> 00:30:36.118
It's a shame though.

00:30:36.161 --> 00:30:37.594
She was about to make
the biggest discovery

00:30:37.630 --> 00:30:38.722
in human history.

00:30:38.764 --> 00:30:40.095
It could have changed
her career.

00:30:40.132 --> 00:30:41.258
And ended ours.

00:30:41.300 --> 00:30:42.995
I am curious, Lieutenant.

00:30:43.102 --> 00:30:44.865
What does it mean..."groovy"?

00:30:44.903 --> 00:30:46.564
Hey! Hey, you guys!

00:30:46.605 --> 00:30:47.663
Red Alert!

00:30:48.707 --> 00:30:51.107
Hey! Hey!

00:30:51.143 --> 00:30:53.304
Just wait a minute!

00:30:53.345 --> 00:30:55.313
What the hell
did you do to my computer?

00:30:55.347 --> 00:30:56.712
It is screwed up!

00:30:56.749 --> 00:30:58.182
The hard drive is wiped.

00:30:58.217 --> 00:30:59.775
Look, I don't have
time to explain.

00:30:59.818 --> 00:31:01.183
Who are you people

00:31:01.220 --> 00:31:03.279
and what is that thing
in your pants?

00:31:03.322 --> 00:31:04.346
I beg your pardon?

00:31:04.390 --> 00:31:05.948
That little gadget
you put in your pocket.

00:31:06.058 --> 00:31:07.616
What is it, a demagnetizer?

00:31:07.660 --> 00:31:08.592
Get down!

00:31:14.333 --> 00:31:15.300
What the hell?!

00:31:15.334 --> 00:31:16.301
Do you have a car?

00:31:16.335 --> 00:31:17.302
Yeah, over there.

00:31:17.336 --> 00:31:18.826
We will need to use it.

00:31:37.089 --> 00:31:37.748
Here!

00:31:47.466 --> 00:31:50.094
Operations Officer's Log,
supplemental.

00:31:50.135 --> 00:31:52.160
We've been on full sensor alert
looking for signs

00:31:52.204 --> 00:31:54.297
that anyone else
has detected Voyager.

00:31:54.340 --> 00:31:56.934
As a precaution,
I've also asked Neelix and Kes

00:31:56.975 --> 00:31:59.136
to monitor all media broadcasts.

00:32:01.146 --> 00:32:02.511
We've set up
a computer algorithm

00:32:02.548 --> 00:32:04.140
to search for key
words and phrases...

00:32:04.183 --> 00:32:05.912
anything that might
indicate Voyager.

00:32:05.951 --> 00:32:06.918
Anything so far?

00:32:06.952 --> 00:32:08.317
Not yet.

00:32:08.354 --> 00:32:10.219
Although we have come across

00:32:10.255 --> 00:32:13.053
some very intriguing
televised broadcasts.

00:32:13.092 --> 00:32:14.957
Take a look at this.

00:32:14.993 --> 00:32:18.622
It's a form of entertainment
called a soap opera.

00:32:18.664 --> 00:32:22.964
The exploration of human
relationships is fascinating.

00:32:23.001 --> 00:32:25.970
Hmm. I can't imagine
just watching the story

00:32:26.071 --> 00:32:27.504
and not being a part of it.

00:32:27.539 --> 00:32:30.633
That's because you've been
spoiled by the holodeck.

00:32:30.676 --> 00:32:31.802
There's something to be said

00:32:31.844 --> 00:32:33.869
for noninteractive stories
like this...

00:32:33.912 --> 00:32:35.709
being swept away
in the narrative.

00:32:35.748 --> 00:32:39.309
Oh, I can't wait to see
if Blaine's twin brother

00:32:39.351 --> 00:32:41.979
is the father of Jessica's baby.

00:32:42.087 --> 00:32:43.452
Good work.

00:32:43.489 --> 00:32:44.820
Keep me informed

00:32:44.857 --> 00:32:46.722
and don't get too swept away.

00:32:46.759 --> 00:32:47.987
Uh, aye, sir.

00:32:48.026 --> 00:32:49.288
Nobody'll know the difference.

00:32:49.328 --> 00:32:50.295
I'll know, Sharon.

00:32:50.329 --> 00:32:51.523
He's my brother.

00:32:51.563 --> 00:32:54.828
How can I face him knowing
that our son is his son?

00:32:54.867 --> 00:32:56.630
All you need to know, Jack,

00:32:56.668 --> 00:32:58.260
is that I love you.

00:33:27.399 --> 00:33:28.457
So far, so good.

00:33:28.500 --> 00:33:30.127
We haven't set off any alarms.

00:33:50.222 --> 00:33:52.656
Our Mr. Starling
has built himself

00:33:52.691 --> 00:33:54.124
quite a corporate empire.

00:33:54.159 --> 00:33:56.525
Looks like he's got
wealth, celebrity...

00:33:56.562 --> 00:33:58.826
and an ego to match.

00:34:18.183 --> 00:34:20.515
I see you never learned to type.

00:34:20.552 --> 00:34:22.383
Turn-of-the-millennium
technology wasn't

00:34:22.421 --> 00:34:24.548
a required course
at the Academy.

00:34:24.590 --> 00:34:26.455
This is like stone knives
and bearskins.

00:34:26.492 --> 00:34:27.459
Well, this isn't.

00:34:27.493 --> 00:34:29.120
I'm detecting a force field.

00:34:29.161 --> 00:34:31.288
I can't scan beyond this wall.

00:34:31.330 --> 00:34:34.299
I don't see an access port
or a control panel.

00:34:34.333 --> 00:34:36.699
Maybe we can find something
in his computer.

00:34:40.138 --> 00:34:42.106
He's got a massive
database here,

00:34:42.140 --> 00:34:44.938
but it's protected
by an encryption sequence.

00:34:44.977 --> 00:34:47.104
I'm going to try
interfacing my tricorder.

00:34:52.683 --> 00:34:54.548
Looks like a series
of pictographs.

00:34:54.584 --> 00:34:56.415
They must have used
symbols to represent

00:34:56.453 --> 00:34:58.546
the different functions
of the computer.

00:34:58.588 --> 00:35:02.649
Let's see what Henry's been
up to all these years.

00:35:07.898 --> 00:35:10.833
The transtators were disrupted
by that energy weapon.

00:35:10.867 --> 00:35:12.698
Our communicators are useless.

00:35:12.736 --> 00:35:14.704
That means we can't call the...

00:35:14.738 --> 00:35:16.831
our friends.

00:35:16.873 --> 00:35:18.272
What do we do now?

00:35:18.308 --> 00:35:20.435
You're going to take
a right at the next light

00:35:20.477 --> 00:35:22.035
and a left at the taco stand,

00:35:22.079 --> 00:35:23.603
'cause you're taking me home.

00:35:23.647 --> 00:35:25.672
And you're not keeping the van.

00:35:25.716 --> 00:35:26.683
I am afraid

00:35:26.717 --> 00:35:28.344
that is not possible,
Miss Robinson.

00:35:28.385 --> 00:35:29.943
Your life may be in danger.

00:35:30.053 --> 00:35:32.715
I'm going to pop this hatch
and I'm going to start screaming

00:35:32.756 --> 00:35:34.815
until you tell me
what's going on.

00:35:34.858 --> 00:35:35.950
Who are you?

00:35:36.026 --> 00:35:37.823
What is that thing in orbit?

00:35:37.861 --> 00:35:38.953
Why did that guy try to kill us?

00:35:38.995 --> 00:35:40.895
I told you we're secret agents.

00:35:42.032 --> 00:35:43.966
I'm opening the hatch.

00:35:44.701 --> 00:35:46.862
Look, we saved your life.

00:35:46.903 --> 00:35:48.871
Isn't it obvious
we're on your side?

00:35:48.905 --> 00:35:50.429
I'm standing up.

00:35:50.474 --> 00:35:52.203
I'm taking a deep breath!

00:35:52.242 --> 00:35:54.403
Rain, you're not
going to scream!

00:35:54.444 --> 00:35:56.207
Now, I know you're frightened

00:35:56.246 --> 00:35:57.736
and you've seen
some pretty strange things,

00:35:57.781 --> 00:35:59.681
but you have to trust me.

00:35:59.716 --> 00:36:01.684
We're not going to hurt you

00:36:01.718 --> 00:36:03.208
and I will explain everything.

00:36:03.253 --> 00:36:04.811
It's either that
or take your chances

00:36:04.855 --> 00:36:06.550
with the guy
who tried to vaporize you!

00:36:13.830 --> 00:36:14.990
The UFO... what is it?

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:19.161
It's a Soviet spy satellite.

00:36:19.202 --> 00:36:21.170
Part of a massive KGB operation.

00:36:21.204 --> 00:36:22.262
We're trying to stop it.

00:36:22.305 --> 00:36:24.034
Soviet?

00:36:24.074 --> 00:36:26.838
The USSR broke up
five years ago.

00:36:26.877 --> 00:36:29.243
The KGB doesn't
even exist anymore.

00:36:30.480 --> 00:36:32.038
That's what they'd
like you to think.

00:36:32.082 --> 00:36:34.607
Perhaps we've told her
enough for now.

00:36:34.651 --> 00:36:36.744
What about you, Agent Tuvok?

00:36:36.787 --> 00:36:38.379
What's up with those ears?

00:36:38.421 --> 00:36:39.547
Thought I didn't notice?

00:36:39.589 --> 00:36:41.386
I did.

00:36:41.424 --> 00:36:42.823
What about your weapons?

00:36:42.859 --> 00:36:44.656
What are they... lasers?

00:36:44.694 --> 00:36:45.683
I'm sorry.

00:36:45.729 --> 00:36:47.356
That information is classified,

00:36:47.397 --> 00:36:51.128
and as for my ears,
they are a family trait.

00:36:51.168 --> 00:36:53.432
He's very sensitive about them.

00:36:53.470 --> 00:36:54.767
Oh, whatever.

00:36:56.039 --> 00:37:00.908
We must find a way
to contact our... friends.

00:37:02.946 --> 00:37:04.607
Incredible.

00:37:04.648 --> 00:37:06.377
Starling's computer
designs were inspired

00:37:06.416 --> 00:37:08.714
by technology from the timeship.

00:37:11.254 --> 00:37:15.384
He introduced the very first
isograted circuit in 1969,

00:37:15.425 --> 00:37:18.019
two years after Braxton's
ship crash-landed.

00:37:18.061 --> 00:37:19.392
And every few years,
there's been

00:37:19.429 --> 00:37:21.863
an equally revolutionary
advance in computers...

00:37:21.898 --> 00:37:23.695
all from Chronowerx Industries,

00:37:23.733 --> 00:37:26.361
all based on Starling's
crude understanding

00:37:26.403 --> 00:37:28.337
of 29th-century technology.

00:37:28.371 --> 00:37:31.204
Are you thinking what
I'm thinking, Chakotay?

00:37:31.241 --> 00:37:32.799
I wish I weren't.

00:37:32.843 --> 00:37:35.368
The computer age
of the late 20th century...

00:37:35.412 --> 00:37:36.504
Shouldn't have happened.

00:37:36.546 --> 00:37:38.707
But it did, and it's
part of our history,

00:37:38.748 --> 00:37:41.410
all because of that timeship.

00:37:42.452 --> 00:37:43.419
Look at this.

00:37:43.453 --> 00:37:45.944
Gantry, power conduits,
telemetry consoles.

00:37:46.022 --> 00:37:48.115
This looks like a design
for a launching bay.

00:37:48.158 --> 00:37:49.125
Braxton was right.

00:37:49.159 --> 00:37:50.353
The ship's going to be launched.

00:37:50.393 --> 00:37:51.519
We've got to send
these schematics

00:37:51.561 --> 00:37:52.528
to Voyager for analysis.

00:37:52.562 --> 00:37:53.790
Janeway to Voyager.

00:37:53.830 --> 00:37:54.956
Kim here, Captain.

00:37:54.998 --> 00:37:56.295
We're in Starling's office.

00:37:56.333 --> 00:37:58.324
I want you to establish
a com-link with my tricorder

00:37:58.368 --> 00:38:00.495
and try to upload
his computer database.

00:38:00.537 --> 00:38:02.437
Aye, Captain.
We'll need a few minutes

00:38:02.472 --> 00:38:04.406
to reconfigure
to their binary system.

00:38:04.441 --> 00:38:05.738
Acknowledged.

00:38:05.775 --> 00:38:07.265
Let's see if we can find out

00:38:07.310 --> 00:38:09.278
where the location
of that launch pad is.

00:38:11.281 --> 00:38:12.578
You're really getting
the hang of this.

00:38:12.616 --> 00:38:13.674
I'm a quick study.

00:38:13.717 --> 00:38:16.447
You know, Captain, in a way,
Braxton was right.

00:38:16.486 --> 00:38:18.920
If we hadn't fought him when
he tried to destroy Voyager,

00:38:19.022 --> 00:38:21.081
he wouldn't have been
pulled back in time,

00:38:21.124 --> 00:38:22.682
his ship wouldn't have
crash-landed on Earth

00:38:22.726 --> 00:38:24.853
and none of this
would have happened.

00:38:24.895 --> 00:38:26.157
Time travel.

00:38:26.196 --> 00:38:28.323
Since my first day on the job
as a Starfleet Captain,

00:38:28.365 --> 00:38:29.889
I swore I'd never let
myself get caught

00:38:29.933 --> 00:38:32.367
in one of these
godforsaken paradoxes.

00:38:32.402 --> 00:38:34.131
The future is the past,
the past is the future.

00:38:34.170 --> 00:38:35.569
It all gives me a headache.

00:38:35.605 --> 00:38:36.594
Hold on.

00:38:37.641 --> 00:38:38.608
This looks promising.

00:38:38.642 --> 00:38:40.837
Try "timeship security portal."

00:38:40.877 --> 00:38:43.368
Maybe it's linked to some sort
of surveillance system.

00:38:43.413 --> 00:38:46.041
An image of the launch bay
would give us a clue

00:38:46.082 --> 00:38:47.447
to its location.

00:39:02.332 --> 00:39:05.130
I see you've made yourself
at home.

00:39:05.168 --> 00:39:08.160
Welcome to the 20th century.

00:39:14.344 --> 00:39:16.278
I know who you are.

00:39:16.313 --> 00:39:18.372
You're from the future.

00:39:18.415 --> 00:39:20.645
I knew you'd come back one day.

00:39:20.684 --> 00:39:23.312
I detected your vessel in orbit

00:39:23.353 --> 00:39:25.844
and Mr. Dunbar, here,
had a run-in

00:39:25.889 --> 00:39:27.186
with your friends.

00:39:27.223 --> 00:39:30.192
You're here
to take the timeship.

00:39:30.226 --> 00:39:31.853
Mr. Starling,

00:39:31.895 --> 00:39:35.558
you're about to cause
a terrible disaster

00:39:35.598 --> 00:39:37.725
that will affect
the 29th century,

00:39:37.767 --> 00:39:41.134
an explosion that will cost
billions of lives.

00:39:41.171 --> 00:39:43.366
We're here to stop you
from doing that.

00:39:44.741 --> 00:39:46.538
What are you talking about?

00:39:46.576 --> 00:39:48.771
If you launch that ship
and travel to the future,

00:39:48.812 --> 00:39:51.542
it will destroy
Earth's solar system.

00:39:51.581 --> 00:39:54.049
How do you know this?

00:39:54.084 --> 00:39:55.051
Well, let's just say,

00:39:55.085 --> 00:39:57.519
we talked to the ship's
previous owner.

00:39:57.554 --> 00:39:59.385
He told us that
if its temporal matrix

00:39:59.422 --> 00:40:01.617
isn't precisely calibrated,

00:40:01.658 --> 00:40:04.491
you'll trigger
a temporal explosion.

00:40:04.527 --> 00:40:05.687
That ship shouldn't be here.

00:40:05.729 --> 00:40:07.754
It belongs to another century.

00:40:07.797 --> 00:40:08.889
We have to take it back.

00:40:09.933 --> 00:40:12.231
What's that?

00:40:12.268 --> 00:40:13.860
It's a communication device.

00:40:13.903 --> 00:40:15.393
Someone's trying to contact me.

00:40:16.740 --> 00:40:18.503
Answer it.

00:40:20.443 --> 00:40:21.410
Janeway here.

00:40:21.444 --> 00:40:23.241
Captain, we've established
the com-link.

00:40:23.279 --> 00:40:25.076
Ready to upload on your signal.

00:40:25.115 --> 00:40:26.605
Do it.

00:40:28.218 --> 00:40:29.708
My database.

00:40:29.753 --> 00:40:32.221
Stop or I'll kill your Captain.

00:40:32.255 --> 00:40:33.244
Who is this?

00:40:33.289 --> 00:40:35.553
You've got five seconds.

00:40:35.592 --> 00:40:36.991
Break the link.

00:40:37.027 --> 00:40:38.756
Done.

00:40:38.795 --> 00:40:40.695
What's our transporter status?

00:40:40.730 --> 00:40:43.358
The main pattern buffers
are still off-line.

00:40:43.400 --> 00:40:46.233
We can try an emergency
transport from a lower orbit.

00:40:46.269 --> 00:40:48.635
That's exactly what the Captain
ordered us not to do.

00:40:48.671 --> 00:40:49.638
We'd be risking detection.

00:40:49.672 --> 00:40:51.162
Harry, we can't worry
about that now.

00:40:51.207 --> 00:40:52.333
Their lives are in danger.

00:40:52.375 --> 00:40:54.741
And if somebody sees a starship
flying through the clouds?

00:40:54.778 --> 00:40:56.245
The Captain put you in charge.

00:40:56.279 --> 00:40:57.541
It is your decision.

00:41:01.551 --> 00:41:03.542
Helm, get a fix on Chakotay
and the Captain.

00:41:03.586 --> 00:41:04.553
Aye, sir.

00:41:04.587 --> 00:41:06.054
B'Elanna, stand by
emergency transporters.

00:41:06.089 --> 00:41:08.489
Get ready to beam them
directly to the Bridge.

00:41:09.692 --> 00:41:11.250
Take us down.

00:41:14.297 --> 00:41:18.290
You've taken over 3,000
gigabytes of information

00:41:18.334 --> 00:41:20.734
including my launch plan,

00:41:20.770 --> 00:41:24.262
but that's not going
to be a problem, Captain.

00:41:24.307 --> 00:41:27.674
I'll make a few changes
to my travel itinerary.

00:41:27.710 --> 00:41:29.439
You're not going to stop me.

00:41:29.479 --> 00:41:33.313
If you don't give us that ship,
we'll take it by force.

00:41:33.349 --> 00:41:37.445
In case you haven't noticed,
I'm holding the gun.

00:41:37.487 --> 00:41:40.320
Not for long.

00:41:40.356 --> 00:41:41.983
I've got a starship in orbit

00:41:42.058 --> 00:41:44.424
that could vaporize
this entire building

00:41:44.461 --> 00:41:46.656
in the blink of an eye.

00:41:46.696 --> 00:41:48.687
And you along with it.

00:41:48.731 --> 00:41:51.165
If necessary.

00:41:51.201 --> 00:41:55.661
Captain, you've got
some cojones.

00:41:57.807 --> 00:41:58.535
Kill them!

00:41:59.576 --> 00:42:01.635
Damn.

00:42:06.149 --> 00:42:07.616
Helm, maintain present altitude.

00:42:07.650 --> 00:42:08.947
Keep us
within transporter range.

00:42:08.985 --> 00:42:10.145
Chakotay, see if you can disable

00:42:10.186 --> 00:42:11.448
the force field
around that timeship.

00:42:11.488 --> 00:42:13.388
B'Elanna, prepare to lock on
to the timeship

00:42:13.423 --> 00:42:15.186
and beam it to Cargo Bay 2.

00:42:15.225 --> 00:42:17.693
Ensign Kim, you have
an impeccable sense of timing.

00:42:17.727 --> 00:42:19.888
Not bad for your first day
in the big chair.

00:42:22.532 --> 00:42:24.193
The force field's down.

00:42:26.035 --> 00:42:27.093
Sir! The timeship!

00:42:30.874 --> 00:42:33.240
They're trying
to teleport the ship.

00:42:34.878 --> 00:42:36.811
The matter stream
is remodulating.

00:42:36.944 --> 00:42:39.003
He's disrupting transport.

00:42:41.749 --> 00:42:43.376
Yes.

00:42:44.552 --> 00:42:46.679
Captain, I don't understand how,

00:42:46.720 --> 00:42:49.382
but he's using our transporter
beam as a downlink.

00:42:49.423 --> 00:42:51.391
He's accessing
our main computer.

00:42:56.096 --> 00:42:57.996
Every time I try
to disable his downlink,

00:42:58.032 --> 00:42:59.966
he comes up
with a new command override.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:03.060
Starling is using 29th-century
technology against us.

00:43:03.103 --> 00:43:04.536
We may not be able
to keep up with him.

00:43:07.107 --> 00:43:09.234
Inertial dampers are off-line.

00:43:09.276 --> 00:43:10.800
He's gotten into
our propulsion systems.

00:43:15.216 --> 00:43:16.581
Disengage transporters.

00:43:16.617 --> 00:43:18.346
Destabilizing matter stream.

00:43:18.385 --> 00:43:20.478
Transporters off-line.

00:43:20.521 --> 00:43:22.955
We've terminated
the downlink, Captain,

00:43:23.023 --> 00:43:25.890
but he got at least 20 percent
of our main computer data files.

00:43:25.926 --> 00:43:27.757
Get us back into orbit
and I want a full damage...

00:43:27.795 --> 00:43:31.754
Captain Janeway...
Henry Starling here.

00:43:31.799 --> 00:43:33.232
This is Janeway.

00:43:33.267 --> 00:43:34.234
USS Voyager...

00:43:34.268 --> 00:43:36.133
Intrepid-class.

00:43:36.170 --> 00:43:37.967
Much bigger than I expected...

00:43:38.005 --> 00:43:39.165
and much less advanced.

00:43:39.206 --> 00:43:44.940
Says here your ship was launched
in the year... 2371?

00:43:44.979 --> 00:43:46.844
You're from the 24th century?

00:43:46.881 --> 00:43:49.816
And here all this time, I
thought you were from the 29th.

00:43:49.850 --> 00:43:52.444
Looks like I have
the home-field advantage.

00:43:52.486 --> 00:43:56.217
Ooh, what's this?

00:43:56.257 --> 00:43:57.485
Oh, now, this is intere...

00:43:58.525 --> 00:44:00.117
Damage reports are coming in.

00:44:00.160 --> 00:44:02.924
Some minor power fluctuations
in the impulse drive

00:44:02.963 --> 00:44:06.091
and a few burned-out circuits
in the main computer core.

00:44:06.133 --> 00:44:07.157
Nothing we can't handle.

00:44:07.201 --> 00:44:08.225
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:44:08.269 --> 00:44:09.759
Captain,
I can't find the Doctor.

00:44:09.803 --> 00:44:11.703
Is his program off-line?

00:44:11.739 --> 00:44:13.730
No. His program is gone.

00:44:15.242 --> 00:44:17.472
Where am I?

00:44:17.511 --> 00:44:19.741
Who are you?

00:44:19.780 --> 00:44:21.839
Welcome.

00:44:21.882 --> 00:44:23.941
Captain, this is Neelix.

00:44:24.051 --> 00:44:25.712
There's something
on the television

00:44:25.753 --> 00:44:27.243
I think you should see.

00:44:27.288 --> 00:44:29.950
It's a current events program.

00:44:29.990 --> 00:44:32.424
I asked Neelix to monitor
Earth broadcasts.

00:44:32.459 --> 00:44:34.620
I'm transferring it
to the main viewer.

00:44:34.662 --> 00:44:36.630
Incredible footage was caught
just an hour ago

00:44:36.664 --> 00:44:38.131
by a man using his camcorder

00:44:38.165 --> 00:44:40.292
to tape a backyard barbecue.

00:44:40.334 --> 00:44:42.825
The massive, unidentifiable
object does not appear

00:44:42.870 --> 00:44:45.395
to be a meteorite, weather
balloon or satellite,

00:44:45.439 --> 00:44:47.464
and one aviation expert
we've spoken to

00:44:47.508 --> 00:44:49.169
has stated that it's definitely

00:44:49.209 --> 00:44:51.336
not any kind of U.S. Aircraft
currently in use.

00:44:51.378 --> 00:44:52.675
We're awaiting investigation

00:44:52.713 --> 00:44:55.477
by local authorities,
and we'll keep you updated

00:44:55.516 --> 00:44:57.952
as news develops
on this incredible story...
